# Everything in this repo is consumed by Linux tooling: shell scripts run inside
# containers, `patch` matches context lines byte-for-byte, and make parses recipes.
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, which checks files out with
# CRLF and breaks all three:
#
#   build.sh   -> /usr/bin/env: 'sh\r': No such file or directory
#   *.patch    -> context lines stop matching; the backport silently fails to apply
#   Makefile   -> recipe parsing errors
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree makes the build behave identically on Windows,
# macOS and Linux regardless of the cloner's git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Binary artefacts - never touch these
*.pdf  binary
*.deb  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary
